  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the collapsed title, once a main screen has scrolled, shown in a **pill centred at the top** in the free space between the floating buttons, as the Claude iOS app shows its conversation title, so that the title stays readable and matches the Liquid Glass buttons around it.\n\n### Continuation of #977 (operator, 2026-11-16)\n\n- #977: the large title at landing, collapsing on scroll.\n- **This issue:** the collapsed state. Instead of a plain inline title, a **glass pill centred horizontally** in the top bar's free space, between the left button (account, or back) and the right buttons (refresh, « ⋯ », compose).\n- Reference: the Claude iOS app's top bar (operator's screenshot, kept locally): a centred capsule with the title on one line, truncated with « … », and a secondary line in it when the screen has a subtitle.\n\n### Wanted\n\n- The pill is Liquid Glass, the same family as the floating buttons, with the same height as those buttons.\n- The title fits on one line, ending with « … » when long. The pill's width follows the free space; it never overlaps the buttons.\n- It applies to the root screens of #977 (Favoris, Messages, Réglages, Catégories). Whether the pushed screens (a forum's topic list, the reader, whose title is already inline) adopt it too: propose it in the PR with screenshots; the operator decides.\n- Coordinate with #865 (the title gets out of the way when scrolling down): one PR for #977, this issue and #865 if they share the top-bar code.\n- VoiceOver keeps the title as the screen's header.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Collapsed: a centred pill, no overlap with the buttons in portrait, in landscape, on a Pro Max and on iPad. Large at landing (#977).\n- [ ] A test on the layout rule (the pill's width from the free space, truncation) fails without the change.\n- [ ] Device check in the general review.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
